  "proof": [
    "Every candidate has D*p=N with positive in-band p.",
    "REPEATED_LOWER has p>=ceil(L/r^2) and |N|<=24+Q_max*max(|2*T_min-2*r-1|,|2*T_max-2*r-1|).",
    "REPEATED_UPPER has p>=ceil(L/Q_max) and |N|<=max(|12+r^2*(2*r+1-2*T_min)|,|12+r^2*(2*r+1-2*T_max)|).",
    "Therefore |D|=|N|/p<=N_bound/p_min<floor(N_bound/p_min)+1, so bisecting Q in 2*r^2 plus or minus that integer width cannot omit an in-band algebraic tuple."
